WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
So now, I want to take up in May the 25th, 1912, is that right?

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.960
Yes.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.960
Okay.

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:15.520
So the soul who lives in the divine will is a soft object in the hands of Jesus.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.680
Soft object means malleable.

6
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.240
We would use the term malleable.

7
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:28.480
So malleable means that God can actually work with us.

8
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.400
So Louisa says, "This morning my beloved Jesus, seeing me very oppressed, let me suckle from

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.840
his heart."

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.880
And then he told me, "Now notice, let me suckle from his heart.

11
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.600
She's using an image that doesn't fit."

12
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.400
Is that okay?

13
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.960
Because the images of a child suckling from a breast, and this is where you can misinterpret

14
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.760
her writings.

15
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:59.080
We would say, "Allowed me to draw from his heart," the way we would express it.

16
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.080
Okay.

17
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.960
So Jesus said, "My daughter, if one wants to make a hole in a hard object, or give it

18
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.560
another shape, that object would be ruined and shattered."

19
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:17.560
But if it is soft and made of a malleable pace, you see where I got my word?

20
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:22.720
One can make the hole, or give it the shape destined without fearing that it might break.

21
00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.760
So putting a hole in a piece of pudding is not a problem.

22
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.400
Putting it in a piece of iron, you've got to be very careful.

23
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.840
And if we wanted to give back the original shape, that object would be ready for everything

24
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.800
with no difficulty, in other words, your malleable.

25
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.640
Such is the soul who lives in my will.

26
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.640
She is a soft object, and I can make of her whatever I want.

27
00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.900
The next sentence is now this, now that and now the other, which is not English, so sometimes

28
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:59.440
I would wound her, or I would embellish her.

29
00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:07.120
I might even enlarge her, or in one instant I could remake her again.

30
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.240
And the soul is ready for everything.

31
00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:15.160
She opposes nothing, and I must carry her in my hands, delighting in her continuously.

32
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:23.280
So put at the side of that surrender, this is utter surrender that is being described,

33
00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.040
surrender to God.

34
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:38.840
So May the 30th, 1912, for the soul who truly loves Jesus, there cannot be separation from

35
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:39.840
him.

36
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:46.840
So all these writings, a very simple statement is made, and that is love is union.

37
00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.960
Love is union.

38
00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:57.960
So if for someone who truly loves God, there has to be that union there, at some level,

39
00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.200
and love forms their mutual rest.

40
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.760
So continuing in my usual state, I fell to a press because of the privation of my beloved

41
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.760
Jesus.

42
00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.440
So I could go on from that.

43
00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:16.400
He said, "My daughter, when you are without me," now she cannot be without him, because

44
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.280
if the divine will leaves us, we disintegrate, okay?

45
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.440
We can only survive if the divine will is in us.

46
00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:30.160
We cannot be without him if we're in grace because the Lord indwells each one of us.

47
00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.720
Isn't that right?

48
00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:36.480
So when he says to her, "When you are without me," he's talking about the deprivation that

49
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.360
she doesn't see him with her eyes, okay?

50
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:48.320
He said, "Make use of this very privation to double or triple to increase a hundred-fold

51
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.520
your acts of love towards me."

52
00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:56.080
Now what he's saying here is, "When you're not feeling wonderful about prayer and you

53
00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:00.840
feel you can't do it, that's the time when you multiply your prayers, whereas we're

54
00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.640
inclined to do the opposite.

55
00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.360
We wait until we feel good about it, and then we multiply the prayers."

56
00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.120
And he says, "No, it is actually more valued the other way around, because the other way

57
00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.520
around you're showing much more trust in God."

58
00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.520
Okay.

59
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.920
So when you have the deprivation, you increase your prayers a hundred-fold.

60
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:26.920
In such a way as to form an environment, all of love inside and outside of you, in which

61
00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.520
you will find me.

62
00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:35.320
Now God is love, one John four seven, okay?

63
00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:46.200
And Sam one four five, verse seventeen, God only ever acts out of love.

64
00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:52.020
So if we don't have an environment of love in our relationship with God, there is no

65
00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.960
union.

66
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:59.280
And you might say how on earth could anybody be religious and not have a relationship with

67
00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.280
God.

68
00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:05.840
The thing is millions have, in other words, they can go to church and they can attend

69
00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.840
services and they can say prayers, but the whole thing is outside of themselves.

70
00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.720
They are not interiorly communing with God.

71
00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.720
Is that okay?

72
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:24.940
Now you get a very good example of that in the parable of the Pharisee and the publican.

73
00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:34.800
Now that's Luke, what is it, I think it sounds like Luke nineteen, where you had this very

74
00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:40.040
religious man telling God that he was the most perfect man on the planet.

75
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.640
And he was telling God also that the one at the door was nothing.

76
00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:49.000
But the one at the door was actually communing with God in truth.

77
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.000
God be merciful to me as sinner.

78
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.400
He was actually connecting with God in truth.

79
00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.880
So you can in fact go through religious services without making the connection with God.

80
00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.640
And you can see it nowadays as well with people coming to church, for example, say at funerals

81
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:10.600
or weddings, and they don't even know when to stand over, sit down or when to say yes,

82
00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:20.560
I or no, there's no connection there, they're just attending a social thing, that's all.

83
00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.160
So there must be an environment, all of love inside and outside of you in which you will

84
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:30.960
find me, you find him in love because he is love.

85
00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:35.880
Now you've heard me say many times that the summary of the thirty six volumes is divine

86
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:41.400
will and love because God is love and God is divine will.

87
00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.360
You will find me more beautiful and as though reborn to new life.

88
00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:50.360
In fact, wherever love is, there I am.

89
00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:52.840
Now we used to sing that in Latin.

90
00:06:52.840 --> 00:07:07.000
Ubi carried us at Amor deus Ibi, as do you remember?

91
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.680
That was one of our favourite hymns in the past when we knew what we were doing in a

92
00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:19.840
church where there is love and charity, there is God because God is love.

93
00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:23.360
So in fact, wherever love is, there I am.

94
00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.760
Therefore, for the soul who truly loves me, there can be no separation.

95
00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:36.400
That's one John three two, one John three two.

96
00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.520
Rather we form the same thing.

97
00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.160
Now that's John fourteen twenty to twenty one.

98
00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:49.120
We form the same thing you in me and I in you.

99
00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:56.000
See there we form the same thing because love seems to create me, to give me life, to nourish

100
00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.240
me and to make me grow.

101
00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:06.400
So when we have an environment of love inside of us, it enables him to be able to by locate

102
00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:12.280
himself in us and to live his true life in us.

103
00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:20.720
In love I find my centre and I feel recreated reborn while I am eternal with no beginning

104
00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.280
and no end.

105
00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:29.500
But thanks to the soul who loves me, I enjoy love so much that I feel as though remade.

106
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:36.160
That means given a new dwelling place on earth to live in.

107
00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:42.120
Just like every time they build a church for Jesus, they give him a new dwelling place to

108
00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.120
live.

109
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:49.920
Every time we open our hearts in love to let him dwell in us in a deeper way, we're giving

110
00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.400
him a new dwelling place.

111
00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:58.360
So furthermore, in this love I find my true rest.

112
00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.040
That's because he is love.

113
00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:06.120
My intelligence rests in the intelligence of the one who loves me.

114
00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.800
My heart rests in the heart of the one who loves me.

115
00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:16.000
My desires, my hands and my feet, they rest in the heart of the one who loves me.

116
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:22.760
In the desire that loves me and the one who desires only me, now desires only me follows

117
00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:26.120
that surrender bit that you're surrendered to him.

118
00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:31.600
And therefore, he is the primary relationship in your life.

119
00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:35.840
In the hands that work for me, in the feet that walk only for me.

120
00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:41.240
So part by part, I go along resting in the soul who loves me.

121
00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:48.360
This is why you'll hear Louisa saying in various places in her writings, I fuse all

122
00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.440
of me in all of him.

123
00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:57.560
Okay, and a very quick way of saying it is, "Jesus, I fuse all of me in all of you all

124
00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.600
the time."

125
00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.080
So it's going on all the time.

126
00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.440
So part by part, I go along resting in the soul who loves me.

127
00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:13.880
And the soul with her love finds me in everything and everywhere.

128
00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:19.320
Now this is your sign that the person is truly in union with God, that you find him everywhere

129
00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:25.640
and in everything, no matter whether it's a problem or whether it's a blessing.

130
00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.880
She rests completely in me.

131
00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:32.280
Now to rest completely in him is Sam 1-3-1.

132
00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.360
And so do a few verses in it.

133
00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.960
My soul is like a weaned child on its mother's lap, and there's nothing more restful than

134
00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:40.680
that.

135
00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.240
Okay.

136
00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:48.280
She rests completely in me, and in my love, she is reborn, she is embellished, and she

137
00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.600
grows in an admirable way in my own love.

138
00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:57.040
Now notice he said that he's reborn in us, and he finds a new dwelling in us, and we

139
00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.920
are reborn in him, and we find the dwelling in him.

140
00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:03.160
It's you and me and I and you, that's your John 14.

141
00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:10.560
Now that text is actually terribly important, and you're told that love makes love, and

142
00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.040
it is in love that we are reborn.

143
00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:21.520
Now in other writings, Jesus often tells us that he has written everything into nature.

144
00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:27.680
For example, he intended you and me to be conceived in love.

145
00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:32.280
He intended you and me to be nurtured in the womb in love.

146
00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:39.480
He intended us to be born in love, to be nurtured in our early years with love, to be put on

147
00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:47.560
our feet with love, and then when we would reach the age of adulthood, that we ourselves

148
00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:53.560
would be able to enter into this union and pass love on to another generation.

149
00:11:53.560 --> 00:12:00.680
That's love being born, nurtured, coming to maturity, and then letting love be reborn,

150
00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:01.680
and so on.

151
00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.320
He's saying the same thing on a spiritual level here.

152
00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:11.600
But you've already experienced it, and this is why you hear me saying often, most of the

153
00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.760
spiritual realities, the Lord has written them into our personal experience.

154
00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:20.120
Now we experience them not on a perfect level to know to be in it, because human beings

155
00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:27.800
are not perfect, but insofar as human beings can express this, you will have experienced

156
00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.880
it in some way.

157
00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:36.520
And so he's saying, "Now I want this reality to be for you permanently on the level of

158
00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.720
the Spirit in your union with God."

159
00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:44.720
Okay, June the 2nd, 1912.

160
00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:49.720
Only the things which are extraneous to Jesus can separate the soul from him.

161
00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.760
Now that might sound a bit funny.

162
00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:59.040
Can I give you a heading to put on a prohibited baggage for your flight?

